          { name: "Treating Unopposed Victory as Mandate for Governance Without Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed race masks whether a constituency is genuinely consolidated or whether opposition is latent and responsive to a credible challenger. A representative who uses the unopposed term to govern without active engagement of the renter constituency, the educated-professional segment, and minority communities is allowing a political vacuum to develop—exactly the context in which a challenger with a more specific constituent-service message becomes viable. The 100% margin is a temporary condition, not a structural feature, and requires active relationship-building to remain durable." }
