          "Lead on education and workforce development as core governance priorities—the 26.2% college-attainment rate and 36.9 median age describe a professional workforce constituency for whom K–12 quality, higher education funding, and skills-training access are direct economic concerns; a representative who makes these issues concrete and urgent commands credibility with the educated plurality.",
          "Build active constituent relationships with the ~4.6% demographic gap and ensure that minority communities have direct access to the representative's office and visible attention in legislative priorities; unopposed victory does not exempt a legislator from the obligation to serve all constituents, and visible neglect of any community segment creates opening for future opposition.",
          "Establish a legislative record on middle-income economic security—housing affordability, healthcare access, and wage trends—that reflects the district's $72,851 median income and professional composition; in the next competitive cycle, a challenger who addresses economic anxiety more directly than an incumbent will find receptive audience among renters and younger professionals evaluating whether current representation is delivering for them."
