          { name: "Assuming Generic Conservative Positioning Sufficient for a Rural Working-Class District", tag: "avoid", why: "A 41-year median age, $58,239 income, and 19% college attainment describe a working-class constituency that evaluates on concrete economic outcomes — job quality, healthcare affordability, cost of living — rather than abstract ideological positioning. A representative who campaigns or legislates as though opposition is impossible, or who relies on partisan identity alone rather than a record of tangible constituent service on economic concerns, will find that an unopposed 2024 does not protect against a challenger who leads with why material conditions have not improved for working families in this district." }
