          "Understand that 59% in an urban district is not a durable floor — it is an actively-held coalition dependent on continued constituent service and responsiveness to the three demographic groups that comprise it; any candidate who consolidates only the white working-class base while neglecting Black and Hispanic community engagement or who campaigns as though 59% is comfortable will find the margin erode in the next competitive cycle."
