          "Address the education gap directly: with only 24.1% college attainment, this is a district where K-12 school quality, vocational training access, and wage-earning pathways without a four-year degree are central to constituent concerns about their children's economic future. School funding, trade program investment, and employer partnerships are the practical governance issues that resonate.",
