          { name: "Unopposed 2024 Status and Future Electoral Vulnerability", tag: "careful", why: "An unopposed 2024 result provides no data on what percentage of actual voters would support Kulkarni in a contested race, creating a specific informational gap about the genuine baseline support. The 55.2% renter rate means more than half the district's households turn over regularly, and new residents arriving into neighborhoods have no inherited relationship with the incumbent. If Republican or independent challengers mobilize around housing cost burden, neighborhood disinvestment, or transit access, the unopposed status offers no evidence of resilience to these challenges. Using this term to build concrete constituent relationships and visible policy accomplishments transforms an unopposed victory from a possible vulnerability into a foundation for durability." },
          { name: "Abstract Partisan Messaging in a Material Benefit District", tag: "avoid", why: "The 12.4% college attainment rate is among the lowest in Kentucky, indicating a constituency that prioritizes direct material benefit, concrete constituent service, and visible representation over abstract ideological messaging. A representative who relies on Democratic messaging while failing to deliver tangible results on housing, neighborhood investment, and working-family economic security will find that registration advantage insufficient to protect against challengers who offer concrete solutions to constituent problems. This district evaluates on what government is actually doing for working families, not on who claims to represent them." },
          { name: "Treating Registration Dominance as Automatic Electoral Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "Democratic registration in KY-HD-40 is clearly strong enough to produce an unopposed result, but registration dominance in high-renter urban neighborhoods is historically volatile because renter populations turn over regularly and new arrivals do not inherit partisan loyalty to the incumbent. A representative who coasts on registration advantage without building active constituent relationships, delivering visible policy results, or engaging the district's institutional base will find that unopposed status evaporating in the next cycle when a credible challenger emerges. The unopposed victory is an opportunity to build durability, not evidence that it already exists." }
