          "Engage directly with the small-business and skilled-trades communities that likely anchor this 24.1% college-attainment, 81.6% homeowner constituency; these voters evaluate on whether state policy is helping them sustain and grow their enterprises and whether their workforce has the training pipeline to stay competitive.",
          "Establish a proactive communication strategy on healthcare costs and insurance affordability; in a district where median age is 42.6 and most households are homeowner-based, rising healthcare premiums and rural hospital viability are direct budget concerns that an incumbent must address with policy specificity, not generic reassurance.",
          "Recognize that the 2.47% Hispanic population, while small, may include growing service-sector and construction-trade workforces; consistent constituent attention to this community—rather than assuming it is politically inactive—builds both goodwill and a credible barrier to Democratic recruitment efforts in future cycles."
