          "Lead with engagement of college-educated and professional-class constituencies on education funding, quality-of-life infrastructure, and property tax fairness: at 30.5% college attainment and $81,290 income, this is a constituency that votes on whether government is delivering public goods and opportunity, not on cultural messaging alone.",
          "Build specific outreach to the Hispanic/Latino community (11.27%) and other non-white populations: the demographic diversification in HD-58 is real and growing, and any candidate who treats these populations as peripheral rather than core constituent groups is leaving votes on the table and creating openings for opposition organizing.",
          "Address renter economics and housing affordability directly: at 26.6% renters in a district with high income and education, this population likely includes young professionals and service-sector workers whose housing costs are rising; specific policy solutions on zoning, development, and rental market transparency distinguish serious candidates from those speaking in abstractions."
