          { name: "Ignoring Renter and Minority Community Economic Concerns as 'Special Interests'", tag: "avoid", why: "In a college-educated, professional-class constituency with a meaningful renter population and Hispanic and Asian communities, addressing housing affordability, healthcare access, and economic opportunity is not partisan appeasement—it is governing for the actual constituency. A representative who treats these material concerns as special-interest demands rather than core constituent needs will find them mobilized by any credible challenger who offers genuine engagement. The unopposed victory may have allowed these communities to become invisible, but their concerns are real and present." }
