          "Engage the college-educated, upper-middle-income constituency on specific economic and governance concerns: education funding, property tax fairness, healthcare costs, and professional workforce retention are the material issues for a 39.1% college-educated, $78,077 median-income district, not abstract conservative positioning.",
          "Develop a specific outreach strategy for the 5.71% Hispanic and 1.28% Asian populations; in a district with no recent opposition, these communities' economic needs, healthcare access concerns, and representation in local governance may have become invisible—and a credible challenger could activate these constituencies by demonstrating attention to their specific concerns.",
          "Monitor and actively cultivate the 33.5% renter population: younger professionals, non-family households, and service-sector workers who may not have inherited Republican loyalty and will evaluate based on whether government is delivering on affordability, healthcare access, and economic opportunity—not partisan default."
