          { name: "Overlooking the 5.23% Hispanic Community", tag: "avoid", why: "At 5.23% of the district, the Hispanic community is large enough to be consequential in a 60-40 race — a 4-5 point shift in Hispanic voter engagement or preference is sufficient to flip a competitive seat. The pattern in Kentucky rural districts is often to treat Hispanic constituents as economically invisible or secondary to the white working-class narrative, missing both a genuine constituent service obligation and a specific electoral vulnerability if a challenger does the outreach work this community requires. The renter rate of 28.7% suggests renters include a meaningful Hispanic subset with distinct housing, employment, and healthcare concerns that deserve active engagement." }
