          "Consolidate minority voter engagement with specificity: the 30.27% Black and 15.95% Hispanic constituencies require ongoing attention to police accountability, education equity, and economic opportunity — not sporadic contact; the ~6.97% demographic gap likely includes Native American residents whose sovereignty and healthcare access concerns deserve explicit legislative attention alongside other minority community priorities.",
          "Activate younger renters and working-age adults through concrete policy delivery: the 35.1 median age and 49.6% renter concentration signal a constituency that evaluates on whether government is producing results on healthcare access, wage floors, and housing stability — not inherited partisan loyalty; demonstrate legislative wins on these issues in every electoral cycle.",
          "Treat the 28% Republican opposition as a floor, not a ceiling for mobilization focus — in a 72-28 district, the risk is not losing persuadable Republicans but demobilization of the Democratic base; invest in turnout infrastructure, community organizing, and direct constituent communication in non-presidential years rather than assuming the margin is durable without active engagement."
