          { name: "Partisan Complacency on Policy Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "A college-educated, young, urban constituency evaluates on whether government is actually delivering on quality-of-life improvements—housing, transit, education, job accessibility—not on partisan identity or abstract ideology. An incumbent who campaigns on Democratic branding without demonstrating tangible progress on the material concerns of renters, young adults, and minority communities risks inviting a credible primary or general challenger who connects more directly to constituent needs. This is an educated constituency that knows the difference between rhetoric and results." }
