          "Lead with housing affordability and renter protections as the primary constituent-facing agenda: in a district with nearly two-thirds renter occupancy, tenant rights, anti-displacement policy, and affordable housing development are not secondary issues—they are the material economic security concerns of the constituency and the foundation for holding the seat against any credible challenge.",
          "Build explicit, accountable relationships with the 14.76% Black, 6.05% Hispanic, and 4.74% Asian communities rather than treating them as automatically Democratic: the college-educated, young profile means these communities are evaluating on whether government is delivering equitable outcomes on education funding, healthcare access, and economic opportunity—not on partisan loyalty alone.",
          "Engage young adult workforce and education concerns with specific policy: the 29.4-year median age and 54.8% college-educated profile signal a constituency interested in student debt relief, apprenticeship pathways, job creation in knowledge sectors, and whether state education funding supports their economic mobility—these are the issues that will determine turnout and support in 2026."
