          { name: "Neglecting Material Economic Concerns in Favor of Partisan Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "A constituency with $41,677 median income, 12.6% college attainment, and 43.9 median age has real household budget constraints and limited margin for error; abstract partisan arguments about government overreach or cultural issues, disconnected from concrete economic outcomes, can read as tone-deaf to voters facing immediate financial pressure. In a deeply rural, economically stressed district, a representative who campaigns on partisan principle without demonstrating tangible progress on cost-of-living, employment, or healthcare concerns creates space for challengers offering more material-focused alternatives." }
