          "Acknowledge and address the Republican lean of the surrounding region directly: a 56% win in a district demographically similar to Republican-held seats across eastern Kentucky means the incumbent is swimming upstream; credibility comes from understanding working-class voters' frustrations with both parties and offering targeted solutions, not from denying the region's partisan direction.",
          "Engage the 32.6% renter constituency on housing cost pressure and tenant protections: one-third of the district rents, and renters at $42,487 household income face acute affordability constraints; specific advocacy on rental affordability, eviction prevention, or utility cost management connects to material household vulnerability.",
          "Do not rely on 56% as a floor: in a demographically Republican district held by a Democrat, the margin is fragile and contingent on incumbent performance; any challenger who can credibly claim the incumbent has failed to deliver on kitchen-table economics or job creation in a low-income, low-education-attainment constituency has a viable path to victory."
