          "Treat the unopposed margin as an opportunity for relationship-building, not complacency: use the current cycle to deepen constituent engagement on the economic concerns that actually drive working-class politics, making it harder for any future Democratic challenger to credibly claim the incumbent has lost touch with the district's material reality."
