          { name: "Assuming the Low College Attainment Rate is a Conservative Asset", tag: "avoid", why: "The 26.9% college attainment rate in KY-SD-20 can be framed by a challenger as evidence that state investment in education and workforce development has failed this constituency's children. Any candidate who defaults to positioning low college attainment as a virtue of working-class authenticity, rather than as a governance problem to be remedied with vocational training and community college affordability, cedes the economic mobility narrative to a challenger who takes that gap seriously as a structural barrier to household advancement." }
