          "Demonstrate public education delivery: with 50.6% college-educated adults and a median age of 39.2, this district includes families with school-age children who evaluate legislators on K-12 funding, teacher pay, and school quality; education outcomes are not a swing issue but a consolidation issue—Berg must show that Democratic state-level control translates into measurable school improvements.",
          "Understand the 40% opposition as educated tax-policy conservatism, not cultural opposition: this is not a district where social conservatism is the driving Republican motivation; instead, higher-income voters may be responding to tax policy, regulatory compliance costs, or specific governance frustrations; Berg's margin will hold if delivery on urban quality-of-life issues outweighs Republican messaging on taxes and regulation.",
          "Do not take 60% as a stable mandate: this is a consolidated Democratic base in a swing state, and while the demographic trend favors Democrats, any perception that Berg is neglecting constituent service, becoming detached from the district's material concerns, or failing to deliver on education and housing will create an opening for a credible Republican challenger to move the margin from 60-40 toward 55-45 or closer."
