          { name: "Taking the 63% Margin for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "While 63-37 is a solid Republican result, the underlying demographic profile — working-class income, older median age, high homeownership with property tax vulnerability — suggests this margin is built on economic alignment, not ideological intensity or demographic lock. Any incumbent who campaigns this seat as though 63% represents a permanent coalition rather than an active consolidation of the homeowner majority's current economic interests will find the margin more vulnerable than it appears if an alternative candidate emerges with credible solutions to the constituency's real economic pressures." }
