          "Engage the non-college-educated young adult constituency on economic mobility: childcare costs, housing affordability, and job training programs that lead to stable employment are the direct policy concerns for a cohort without a college pathway; specificity on these issues distinguishes a serious legislator from partisan messaging.",
          "Monitor the 3.1% demographic gap and the 37% opposition base for any organized challenger or mobilization; while the seat is clearly Republican, the working-class income profile and older-skewing median age mean this constituency is responsive to economic messaging rather than ideologically locked, making it more vulnerable than the 63-37 margin might suggest in an economically pressured cycle.",
          "Avoid abstract fiscal conservatism that fails to distinguish between protecting fixed-income homeowners' tax burdens and cutting services those same households depend on; a legislator who appears to be choosing ideology over pocketbook impact will find the 37% opposition more competitive than the current margin allows."
